        "total_usd": 48,
        "rationale": "42 certified modules carry the substrate (durable store, workflow engine, approval trail, RBAC, citations, document extraction, SLA math, UI shells, Cloud Run operability), so each slice is mostly wiring plus this app's genuinely bespoke logic. The estimates sit well under the per-node $15 runaway guards because composition removes the expensive generation: only the ratio/grading engine, the policy rule set, and the five agent mandates are written from scratch. Total leaves ~$52 of the $100 run envelope for the design phase already in flight (design-options alone guards at $36).",
        "node_notes": {
          "slice-plan": "Derives the vertical slices; bounded planning output, cheapest node in the build phase.",
          "slice-1": "Deal entity + intake form + auth/RBAC + pipeline board skeleton — heaviest composition, lightest bespoke code (persistence-core, postgres-adapter, migrations, forms-engine, auth-basic, rbac, row-level-security, data-table, screen-router).",
          "slice-2": "Document upload, native-text PDF extraction, and the financial spreading agent with per-figure citations — three modules do the plumbing (file-upload, doc-extract, table-extract, citation-tracker) but the spread template and citation binding are bespoke.",
          "slice-3": "Deterministic DSCR/leverage/current-ratio engine and the 5-point grading rubric from GAP-052, plus exhaustive unit tests (REQ-023). Entirely bespoke code with no module to lean on, hence the full allocation despite a narrow surface.",
          "slice-4": "Credit memo agent and policy compliance agent over the versioned rule set from GAP-053, with drafts landing in the accept/edit/reject review UI (versioned-drafts, approval-flow, record-detail).",
          "slice-5": "Tiered approval per GAP-054/GAP-055, decline with adverse-action reason, return-to-stage, and the audit view/export — approval-flow, state-machine, audit-view and export-csv cover most of it.",
          "slice-6": "SLA dashboard with business-day math and escalation owner, portfolio Q&A agent under RBAC-scoped retrieval, and the eval suites for all five agents (sla-timers, dashboard-cards, rag-core, search-index, eval-harness)."
        }
